  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "An evaluation of county-level human development across Poland from 2010 to 2023 combines the traditional scalar Local Human Development Index (LHDI) with a complex-number vector approach and typogram visualisations. Although the overall national LHDI remained largely stable over the 13-year period, the dual method uncovered widening wealth and health disparities, rising welfare and education scores, and a widespread drop in the health sub-index alongside strong urban-rural asymmetries.",
      "why": "By converting multidimensional development components into vectors, the framework allows planners to track compositional shifts and structural trade-offs between health, education, and welfare rather than relying solely on a single aggregated score."
    }
  },
